# literal_translation = When another wayfarer, on meeting me, should say that I had a winnowing fan on my stout shoulder, then he commanded me fix my oar in the earth, and make brilliant offerings to lord Poseidon—a ram and a bull and a boar, that mates with sows—and depart for my home, and offer sacred hecatombs to the immortal gods, who hold broad heaven, to each one in due order.
